Reproducible on iOS Safari and desktop Chrome. Only happens inconsistently on Chrome for me.

## Background

Single line thoughts and multiline thoughts have different line heights for aesthetic reasons. Line height **must** be used, not padding or margin, because only when line-height is clicked will the browser selection be placed in the correct place in the thought.

There is no native way to determine if a thought is multiline, so we infer it from the editable height and font size in [useMultiline](https://github.com/cybersemics/em/blob/5252cb5fdef448b29a74d04beec2aa7fe0d48990/src/components/Editable/useMultiline.ts). 

The goal is to update the `multiline` state as soon as the thought height changes, *before* the first paint. Typically this involves a synchronous `useLayoutEffect`, but as you can see in `useMultiline` there are various timing issues we have to deal with when anticipating when the thought's height has changed. 

We cannot use `ResizeObserver` for performance reasons. 

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Create a thought that goes almost to the end of the line. 
2. Enter a character so that the thought wraps and becomes a multiline thought. 

## Current Behavior

The thought is rendered with the incorrect line height on first paint:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f500618a-56bc-441e-9d00-8f9f85cbdbe0

## Expected Behavior

The thought should be rendered with the correct line height immediately.

## Test

Test multiline line-spacing frame by frame. 

Assert that each frame's line-height matches its content. 

e.g. 

``` await page.evaluate(() => {
  window.__frames = [];
  let frame = 0;

  function captureFrame(ts) {
    window.__frames.push({
      frame: frame++,
      timestamp: ts,
      state: getComputedStyle(document.querySelector('.anim')).transform
    });
    requestAnimationFrame(captureFrame);
  }

  requestAnimationFrame(captureFrame);
});
```
